# Settings UI parity (Knoten-Walk / Attribut-Walk)

Canonical plan: [`docs/plans/settings-ui-parity.md`](../../docs/plans/settings-ui-parity.md).  
Model lock: [`docs/DEVELOPER-ATTRIBUTE-MODEL.md`](../../docs/DEVELOPER-ATTRIBUTE-MODEL.md) (OQ-W6 / Q123).

## Agent rule — Altlasten / debt questions

When asked whether legacy / Altlasten remain:

1. Answer **SoT / concept** and **GUI-Ist** **separately**.
2. `OPEN-QUESTIONS` / OQ-W **decided** ≠ admin UI finished.
3. Prefer the settings-ui-parity matrix + [`q123-migrate-handoff.md`](../../docs/plans/q123-migrate-handoff.md) over “model locked → no debt.”

## Docs

Always update living docs / plans / rules when behavior or design changes (`plan-docs-sync.mdc`). **Do not ask** whether to sync — sync in the same change.

## Locked names

| Term | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| **Knoten-Walk** | Open node → Settings of node + attribute targets to the leaf |
| **Attribut-Walk** | Attribute Options → **same** walk from **target type** |
| **Settings** | Capsule `Settings.data` / `Settings.view` — type defaults on node; override deltas on Relation |
| **Not Settings** | Node Identity/Presentation; attribute edge fields (name, Mult, Bindung, RO, Hide, Default seed) |

From the type node downward, Knoten-Walk and Attribut-Walk are the **same search**.  
Override vs type default = **same keys**, different **storage** (Relation delta vs type node) and **blast radius**.

## GUI Soll

- **One** Settings surface = the walk (even single-node depth 0).
- Do **not** also paint legacy Attribute Options **Choices** + depth-0 **Relation overrides** Preferred/date when the walk covers the attribute (`attributeSettingsWalkCovers` in `tree-admin.js`).
- Label the walk **Settings** (not a second “Composition settings” product concept).
- Node ConfigPage vs attribute walk = **plan later** (node mostly aggregates child Settings already visible on attributes) — do not implement until designed.
- **Preferred default** lives on the **type node** / simple-type config; consumers inherit. **Never** by display name.
- **Settings cascade → paint (locked ≈ 0.0.558):** Walk / type presets (Preferred, Q117, Hide, Mult, Bindung) must reach Preview and nested cells. Nested attribute cell = **type Preferred** — not invent Form when Compact is set. No hardcoding by name/path; renderer-local chrome only for the current layer. See [preview-checkpoints.mdc](preview-checkpoints.mdc).
- **Display Preferred (≈ 0.0.537):** stacked form rows — **Render** / **Converter** / **Validators** (label left, select right); options chrome in the **same control column** under each select; validators table only when set (no empty stub).
- **ChildListRenderer:** Choices / child pick UI only when this Preferred is active — same for every type (Währung, Praefix, Konstanten). No `childNodes` ConfigPage box.
- **MultistepRenderer (≈ 0.0.546):** mode **dialog** | **inline** under Render (meta `_wtt_multistep_mode`; default dialog). Renderer-local — not Settings `treePickerMode` (Q74). Legacy Embedded/embed aliases.

## Do / don’t

- **Do** treat double Choices / missing Settings / node≠attribute Settings chrome as **GUI debt**, not a new model.
- **Do** keep ChildList Choices/Default on **Q90 depth** (≤1 list, ≥2 tree) — same as CatalogChoice; Präfixe stays flat, Basiseinheiten tree.
- **Do** keep edge fields in the Attributes **table row**; keep Identity/Presentation on the node — outside Settings.
- **Do** set default Preferred / renderer on the type (or simple config), not on attribute display names.
- **Do** keep Konstanten/**Präfixe** as locked in [`.cursor/rules/praefixe-catalog-lock.mdc`](praefixe-catalog-lock.mdc) (ChildList + Presentation/multiplikator + Compact leaves — do not regress without ask).
- **Don’t** invent a second Settings model for attributes.
- **Don’t** answer “no Altlasten” based only on OQ decided flags when the admin UI still doubles or omits the walk.
- **Don’t** hard-code product logic by display name (`quantity` / `size` / `Kontakt` / …) — walk and Preferred stay type-driven.

